  "note": "Independent source rejudgment against RFC 7950 Section 9.1: \"Implementations MUST support all lexical representations specified in this document.\" Read all tagged units, their type/default/reference helpers and cited producers. Integer tags exercise +17/17/-17 and legal signed hexadecimal/octal module defaults, with exact normalized values and malformed-notation refusals. Decimal64 tags require the declared signed/integral/fraction forms and exact error classes for invalid forms and restrictions. Binary and bits tags distinguish accepted defined representations from malformed alphabet/padding, lengths and unknown bit names. Reference tags exercise type loading, leafref lexical validation, union-default member selection and both quoted leaf-list-predicate forms versus absent target. canonicalValue still canonicalizes signed/unsigned decimal integers and decimal64, returning other representations unchanged; canonicalKey, sameValue and referenceWalk.instanceExists use it for comparison. Its current exhaustive-ignore directive documents that deliberately narrow normalization switch; no new grammar is introduced. Canonical-comparison-specific tests under other IDs are not silently counted as 9.1-1 tags. Verdict enforced. No execution or recorded-proof freshness was verified here.",
